body:
I tried a simpler template and it worked ... so went back to my original template here and starting taking out the mappings piece by piece to see root cause. 

Eliminating this from the template makes it work as intended...

```
"_timestamp" : {
                    "enabled" : true,
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed",
                    "format" : "date_time",
                    "default": null, 
                    "path" : "timestamp"
                },
```

So for some reason using the _timestamp feature in particular is causing this disappearance of indexes...

In order to circumvent the issue, I took out the _timestamp mapping and replaced it with an explicit "date" property instead.   Here is my new template that does NOT cause this issue:

```
{
    "template" : "test-*",
    "order" : 0,
    "settings" : {
        "number_of_shards" : 4,
        "number_of_replicas" : 0, 
        "refresh_interval": "1s"
    },
    "mappings" : {
        "test-type": {
                "dynamic": false,
                "_all": {
                    "enabled": false
                },
                "_source": {
                    "enabled": false
                },
                "properties": {
                    "timestamp": {
                        "type": "date",
                        "format": "date_time",
                        "store": true,
                        "index": "not_analyzed"
                    },
                    "node": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "store": true,
                        "index": "not_analyzed"
                    },
                    "power": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "store": true,
                        "index": "not_analyzed"
                    }
                }
            }
    }
}
```

Indexes created from this template no longer disappear upon cluster restart.  So -- can work around at least to continue to use ES for my desired schema.  (Doesn't bring back my disappeared indexes though...)

Ok more testing of this issue - seems this mapping being in a template was not part of the issue at all, it's solely due to _timestamp in the mapping.   

I created a new index w/o a template but using _timestamp, put in a document, and it too disappeared on cluster restart.
- Create new index and type.

```
PUT http://localhost:9200/new_index
 {
    "settings" : {
        "index" : {
            "number_of_shards" : 1,
            "number_of_replicas" : 0, 
            "refresh_interval": "1s"
        }
    },
    "mappings": {
        "power": {
            "_timestamp" : {
                "enabled" : true,
                "store": true,
                "index": "not_analyzed",
                "format" : "date_time",
                "default": null, 
                "path" : "timestamp"
            },
            "properties": {
                "node": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed"
                },
                "power": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
- Add a document.

```
PUT http://localhost:9200/new_index/power/1
 {
    "node": "n1111",
    "power": 200,
    "timestamp": 1420737933000
}
```
- Restart cluster ... and **index is missing**...
- Redo the above, using explicit timestamp property instead of _timestamp.

```
PUT http://localhost:9200/new_index
{
    "settings" : {
        "index" : {
            "number_of_shards" : 1,
            "number_of_replicas" : 0, 
            "refresh_interval": "1s"
        }
    },
    "mappings": {
        "power": {
            "properties": {
                "timestamp": {
                    "type": "date",
                    "format": "date_time",
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed"
                },
                "node": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed"
                },
                "power": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "store": true,
                    "index": "not_analyzed"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
- Put in data as before, restart cluster ... and index is there.

issue.body:
> **Note**: this issue won't appear anymore in elasticsearch 1.5 and above because #9104 will disable support for `"default":null`. That being said, I think it would be safer to port this patch to 1.x and master branches.

Step to reproduce:
- Create new index and type.

```
DELETE new_index
PUT new_index
 {
    "mappings": {
        "power": {
            "_timestamp" : {
                "enabled" : true,
                "default": null
            }
        }
    }
}
```
- Add a document

```
PUT new_index/power/1
{
    "foo": "bar"
}
```
- Restart cluster ... and **index is missing**...

```
GET new_index
```

Gives IndexMissingException

Closes #9223.

